- PR Title: feat: Fix match-3 obstacle rendering and stability
- The Problem Solved: Fixed game crashes associated with negative tiers (-1 roads, -2 obstacles) and mapping to textures during match-3 merge resolution, bringing the rendering back to stable and aligning it closer to the target GOAL.png.
- Visuals: [verification_match3_after.png](./verification_match3_after.png), [verification_obstacles.png](./verification_obstacles.png) vs [GOAL.png](./GOAL.png)
- Implementation Journey:
  - Addressed crashes reading `undefined` mapped from PALETTE in `createBuildingMesh` logic by safely handling negative tier values.
  - Set generic placeholder textures (Cobblestone) for negative tier structures so they bypass scaling issues.
  - Exported `resolveMerges` globally in `main.js` to facilitate testing.
  - Verified logic execution and visual stability with provided Python evaluation scripts.
- Tradeoffs & Assumptions:
  - Assumption: The specific aesthetic of negative tier rendering wasn't strictly defined, but ensuring a texture that avoids breaking `PALETTE` bounds was key.
  - Paths Considered: 1. Remap all index logic. 2. Append extra indices for negative values into PALETTE directly. 3. Add explicit clamp or override inside `createBuildingMesh`.
  - Selected Path: Approach 3. It minimally affected existing game design bounds and explicitly guards against UI crashes while ensuring valid object generation.
- Testing Instructions: Open `index.html` locally or start via `python -m http.server 8000`. Place obstacles and ensure they render without freezing the canvas. Ensure merges don't crash when passing negative variables.
- Action Item: `git push origin feature/fix-match3-obstacles && gh pr create --title "feat: Fix match-3 obstacle rendering and stability" --body "$(cat pr_manifest.log)"`
